<SECTION SCID = "T010256A143S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010256A143" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "8Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Cooling General</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The cooling system is a pressurized, forced-circulation water-cooled type, with a bottom bypass type in which the thermostat with bypass valve is integrated with the water inlet.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The cooling fan ON/OFF and fan speed are controlled by the cooling fan computer based on signals from the engine control computer.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By adopting a fully sealed reservoir tank, high gas-liquid separation performance and improved cooling system pressure stability have been achieved, and by optimizing its installation position, the air bleed valve used when filling coolant has been eliminated to improve serviceability.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>For serviceability when replacing coolant, a drain cock for air bleeding is provided on the water inlet.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740149p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "4.972in" />
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740176p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "4.583in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010256A144S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010256A144" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "8Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Radiator</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A lightweight, high-performance cross-flow type aluminum core radiator has been adopted, improving cooling performance and reducing weight.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<SPEC ID = "T010256A144X01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Radiator Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Core Type</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Corrugated Fin</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Fin Pitch [mm]</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>3.0 / 2</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Core Dimensions (Width x Height x Thickness) [mm]</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>675 × 370 × 27</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Dry Weight [kg]</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>3.7</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></SPEC>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010256A145S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010256A145" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "8Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Cooling Fan and Fan Shroud</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Based on signals from the engine control computer, the cooling fan computer steplessly controls the speed of the 2 cooling fans according to the engine condition, driving conditions, A/C operation, etc. By always controlling the cooling fans to the optimum speed, cooling performance has been improved while greatly increasing quietness.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A thin ring fan with a band-shaped ring around its outer circumference has been adopted, increasing rigidity and making the fan lighter and more compact.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740150p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "4.250in" />
</FIGURE>
<SPEC ID = "T010256A145X01" INDSW = "OFF">
